From: Armada SM8250 bring-up <jsbonsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Jul 2026 15:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Input: retroid - double-press Home emits Back (quick-access)

The Retroid Pocket Flip 2 lacks the dedicated Back button that opens
the SteamOS quick-access menu on the Pocket 5 (InputPlumber maps
BTN_BACK -> QuickAccess). Detect a double-press of Home (BTN_MODE)
within 450ms in the MCU report parser and emit a BTN_BACK pulse
alongside it. Userspace approaches (evdev watchers, hidraw sniffing,
InputPlumber intercept chords) all fail because the compositor and
InputPlumber hold exclusive grabs, and intercept mode locks input by
design; the driver is the one place that reliably sees the raw button.

Applies to both RP5 and Flip 2, giving a consistent double-tap-Home
gesture for the quick-access menu.
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/retroid.c	2026-07-10 15:10:07
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/retroid.c	2026-07-10 15:11:19
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/input.h>
+#include <linux/jiffies.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
@@ -245,7 +246,30 @@
 	bitmap_xor(&changes, &current_states, &prev_states, ARRAY_SIZE(keymap));
 
 	for_each_set_bit(i, &changes, ARRAY_SIZE(keymap)) {
-		input_report_key(indev, keymap[i], (current_states & BIT(i)));
+		bool pressed = !!(current_states & BIT(i));
+
+		/*
+		 * Double-press Home also emits a Back pulse: the Flip 2 has no
+		 * dedicated Back button, and Back opens the SteamOS quick-access
+		 * menu (InputPlumber maps BTN_BACK -> QuickAccess).
+		 */
+		if (keymap[i] == BTN_MODE && pressed) {
+			static unsigned long last_mode_press;
+
+			if (last_mode_press &&
+			    time_before(jiffies, last_mode_press +
+						msecs_to_jiffies(450))) {
+				input_report_key(indev, BTN_BACK, 1);
+				input_sync(indev);
+				input_report_key(indev, BTN_BACK, 0);
+				input_sync(indev);
+				last_mode_press = 0;
+			} else {
+				last_mode_press = jiffies;
+			}
+		}
+
+		input_report_key(indev, keymap[i], pressed);
 	}
 
 	int16_t value;
